<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani stocks index rises above 1,600 points.</title>
<headline>Pakistani stocks index rises above 1,600 points.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Karachi Stock Exchange 100-share price index rose beyond the 1,600-point barrier to 1,600.51 on Friday on buying of blue chips by foreign investors, dealers said.  </p>
<p>Increased buying of blue chips by foreign investors pushed the index up, a dealer at Ali Husain Rajab Ali said.</p>
<p>Lever Brothers rose 46 rupees to 750.</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
